[{:db/id 17592186119938 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-72828711-fc6d-5cc1-8d14-0b819a351e61"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-72828711-fc6d-5cc1-8d14-0b819a351e61" :question/id #uuid "72828711-fc6d-5cc1-8d14-0b819a351e61" :question/math-academy-id "q-3749" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{-2{x}^{4}+6{x}^{2}-4}{{x}^{2}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{-2{x}^{4}+6{x}^{2}-4}{{x}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{-2(1)^{4}+6(1)^{2}-4}{(1)^{2}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2{x}^{4}+6{x}^{2}-4}{{x}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{-2({x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+2)}{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2({x}^{2}-2)({x}^{2}-1)}{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =-2({x}^{2}-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{-2{x}^{4}+6{x}^{2}-4}{{x}^{2}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\,\\,-2({x}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =-2(1-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2b3845e7-e81e-5c5b-85b8-7d7f11e07468"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2b3845e7-e81e-5c5b-85b8-7d7f11e07468" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b3845e7-e81e-5c5b-85b8-7d7f11e07468" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a6c6b966-6937-5cda-a2a8-2103c125ed81" :answer-field/choices ["answer-edf46e72-237e-5ade-b7c8-d89a1c8c5d81" "answer-8ce5d32b-9d7b-5303-97bb-68e862c5ae64" "answer-a6c6b966-6937-5cda-a2a8-2103c125ed81" "answer-6e1be6ba-0318-5199-9cf7-6cfc2c56fa02" "answer-892f567d-b4cc-5f65-95a7-7373905d09c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-edf46e72-237e-5ade-b7c8-d89a1c8c5d81" :answer/id #uuid "edf46e72-237e-5ade-b7c8-d89a1c8c5d81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ce5d32b-9d7b-5303-97bb-68e862c5ae64" :answer/id #uuid "8ce5d32b-9d7b-5303-97bb-68e862c5ae64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6c6b966-6937-5cda-a2a8-2103c125ed81" :answer/id #uuid "a6c6b966-6937-5cda-a2a8-2103c125ed81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e1be6ba-0318-5199-9cf7-6cfc2c56fa02" :answer/id #uuid "6e1be6ba-0318-5199-9cf7-6cfc2c56fa02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-892f567d-b4cc-5f65-95a7-7373905d09c5" :answer/id #uuid "892f567d-b4cc-5f65-95a7-7373905d09c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119942 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2778d4f8-72c7-5929-98a7-5df304873786" "question-5986bf81-4caa-5e55-8c99-36ab322d7c9c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2778d4f8-72c7-5929-98a7-5df304873786" :question/id #uuid "2778d4f8-72c7-5929-98a7-5df304873786" :question/math-academy-id "q-101160" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{2}+3y-18}{{y}^{2}-3y}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{2}+3y-18}{{y}^{2}-3y} & =\\frac{{3}^{2}+3(3)-18}{{3}^{2}-3(3)}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}+3y-18}{{y}^{2}-3y} & =\\frac{(y+6)(y-3)}{y(y-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+6}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{2}+3y-18}{{y}^{2}-3y} & ={lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{y+6}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3+6}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{3} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-be118eae-f956-5136-8758-541234de46d4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-be118eae-f956-5136-8758-541234de46d4" :answer-field/id #uuid "be118eae-f956-5136-8758-541234de46d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-89b85bb3-22c0-5d24-a29b-0c275ecfe2a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e10ffd2c-df31-5361-8cae-6b39de43c35c" "answer-d56cb5bc-4d9d-5419-a948-dca0397cf746" "answer-81e207e3-fbc2-5800-abe0-1ceefd387562" "answer-89b85bb3-22c0-5d24-a29b-0c275ecfe2a8" "answer-4c83a02a-d899-55c8-a94f-5215ee121e17"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e10ffd2c-df31-5361-8cae-6b39de43c35c" :answer/id #uuid "e10ffd2c-df31-5361-8cae-6b39de43c35c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d56cb5bc-4d9d-5419-a948-dca0397cf746" :answer/id #uuid "d56cb5bc-4d9d-5419-a948-dca0397cf746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81e207e3-fbc2-5800-abe0-1ceefd387562" :answer/id #uuid "81e207e3-fbc2-5800-abe0-1ceefd387562" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89b85bb3-22c0-5d24-a29b-0c275ecfe2a8" :answer/id #uuid "89b85bb3-22c0-5d24-a29b-0c275ecfe2a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c83a02a-d899-55c8-a94f-5215ee121e17" :answer/id #uuid "4c83a02a-d899-55c8-a94f-5215ee121e17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5986bf81-4caa-5e55-8c99-36ab322d7c9c" :question/id #uuid "5986bf81-4caa-5e55-8c99-36ab322d7c9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-313149" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -2}\\frac{{x}^{2}-5x-14}{x+2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}\\frac{{x}^{2}-5x-14}{x+2} & =\\frac{(-2)^{2}-5(-2)-14}{-2+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+10-14}{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-5x-14}{x+2} & =\\frac{(x-7)(x+2)}{x+2} \\\\  & =x-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -2}(x-7) & =(-2)-7 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd8d554e-6195-547e-bcb1-ff6fe5d58358"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd8d554e-6195-547e-bcb1-ff6fe5d58358" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd8d554e-6195-547e-bcb1-ff6fe5d58358" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7b385cd1-b9ce-5705-9e8c-ff293413d49c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7b385cd1-b9ce-5705-9e8c-ff293413d49c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b385cd1-b9ce-5705-9e8c-ff293413d49c" :answer/id #uuid "7b385cd1-b9ce-5705-9e8c-ff293413d49c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-51893726-ddac-5484-9f3a-d915a01dfdcb" :activity/id #uuid "51893726-ddac-5484-9f3a-d915a01dfdcb" :activity/title "Calculating Limits of Rational Functions by Factoring" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049927 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-ec795ac2-9c40-5579-8d71-0f6e0fe67464" "step-6d3de455-eb8b-5f64-94cd-7656cf858b93" "step-c8ebbc60-a13e-5fb9-bd31-db31053b64b4"] :activity/first-step "step-ec795ac2-9c40-5579-8d71-0f6e0fe67464" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-ec795ac2-9c40-5579-8d71-0f6e0fe67464" :step/id #uuid "ec795ac2-9c40-5579-8d71-0f6e0fe67464" :step/content "question-72828711-fc6d-5cc1-8d14-0b819a351e61" :step/next "step-6d3de455-eb8b-5f64-94cd-7656cf858b93" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6d3de455-eb8b-5f64-94cd-7656cf858b93" :step/id #uuid "6d3de455-eb8b-5f64-94cd-7656cf858b93" :step/content "question-2778d4f8-72c7-5929-98a7-5df304873786" :step/next