"answer-9582718d-5732-5f67-8454-d0600cb51fbb" "answer-9f294f0d-3335-520f-be6a-4f7a8fcba641" "answer-05978ef2-526e-513b-a296-30e858ad7d1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-871baed0-e9b4-51b3-b72c-1009d740fb54" :answer/id #uuid "871baed0-e9b4-51b3-b72c-1009d740fb54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4x\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bab7b0e-c8aa-5da1-a567-dc2e839c9038" :answer/id #uuid "6bab7b0e-c8aa-5da1-a567-dc2e839c9038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-3{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9582718d-5732-5f67-8454-d0600cb51fbb" :answer/id #uuid "9582718d-5732-5f67-8454-d0600cb51fbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1+3{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f294f0d-3335-520f-be6a-4f7a8fcba641" :answer/id #uuid "9f294f0d-3335-520f-be6a-4f7a8fcba641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05978ef2-526e-513b-a296-30e858ad7d1a" :answer/id #uuid "05978ef2-526e-513b-a296-30e858ad7d1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1+9{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-db2fa4fe-6b60-51ee-9a41-fc33e6f273b7" :question/id #uuid "db2fa4fe-6b60-51ee-9a41-fc33e6f273b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-341497" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(x-1)] \\\\  & =-4\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{(x-1)\\sqrt{1-(x-1)^{2}}}]\\cdot (x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(x-1)\\sqrt{1-({x}^{2}-2x+1)}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(x-1)\\sqrt{2x-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(x-1)\\sqrt{\\,x(2-x)\\,}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a2e24b88-1d44-5062-9037-62a3b48a7fe6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a2e24b88-1d44-5062-9037-62a3b48a7fe6" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e24b88-1d44-5062-9037-62a3b48a7fe6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0fb02d74-74dc-50e4-a17f-f8ce53c1c0a9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0fb02d74-74dc-50e4-a17f-f8ce53c1c0a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fb02d74-74dc-50e4-a17f-f8ce53c1c0a9" :answer/id #uuid "0fb02d74-74dc-50e4-a17f-f8ce53c1c0a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(x-1)\\sqrt{\\,x(2-x)\\,}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-24bbcf4d-e35e-5166-86db-6c3a81f4f4ca" :question/id #uuid "24bbcf4d-e35e-5166-86db-6c3a81f4f4ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-341493" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-3\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[-3\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)] \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)] \\\\  & =-3\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}]\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b26d762-7065-5240-845a-7fa72921023d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b26d762-7065-5240-845a-7fa72921023d" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b26d762-7065-5240-845a-7fa72921023d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8fa9e367-921c-5703-b5c8-f4ef0ec283c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8fa9e367-921c-5703-b5c8-f4ef0ec283c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fa9e367-921c-5703-b5c8-f4ef0ec283c5" :answer/id #uuid "8fa9e367-921c-5703-b5c8-f4ef0ec283c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186168092 :tutorial/content "The derivatives of the inverse reciprocal hyperbolic functions are shown below:\n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x) & =-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}, &  & x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x) & =-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}, &  & x\\in (0,1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}, &  & x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (1,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the derivative of the base inverse reciprocal hyperbolic functions, we can differentiate combinations of these functions, by using the properties of differentiation.\n\nFor example, let's find the derivative of\n\n$$\ny = \\arsech{(-x^2)}\n$$\n\nUsing the formulas above together with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(-{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{1-{(-{x}^{2})}^{2}}}\\cdot {(-{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}\\cdot (-2x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167021 :activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054812 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0cf33d77-f213-525d-99fb-8b9182428af7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0cf33d77-f213-525d-99fb-8b9182428af7" :question/id #uuid "0cf33d77-f213-525d-99fb-8b9182428af7" :question/math-academy-id "q-12244" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ when $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Writing the radical as a rational exponent, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{1/2}}={x}^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the power rule with $n=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2\\,-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-db460c81-b20d-5e16-92de-4539fa40eda4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-db460c81-b20d-5e16-92de-4539fa40eda4" :answer-field/id #uuid "db460c81-b20d-5e16-92de-4539fa40eda4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fcac43f6-9d84-52e6-bbc3-c7111b1c3113" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fcac43f6-9d84-52e6-bbc3-c7111b1c3113" "answer-a3490041-c6e1-534b-ae84-df116add6226" "answer-f927c200-f0bd-5da8-96d4-fd1b9ab95850" "answer-da522b4a-46a4-5729-803b-4a8ed45b4b35" "answer-f16e8de5-d93f-5c40-b48d-326156982a0f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcac43f6-9d84-52e6-bbc3-c7111b1c3113" :answer/id #uuid "fcac43f6-9d84-52e6-bbc3-c7111b1c3113" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3490041-c6e1-534b-ae84-df116add6226" :answer/id #uuid "a3490041-c6e1-534b-ae84-df116add6226" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f927c200-f0bd-5da8-96d4-fd1b9ab95850" :answer/id #uuid "f927c200-f0bd-5da8-96d4-fd1b9ab95850" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da522b4a-46a4-5729-803b-4a8ed45b4b35" :answer/id #uuid "da522b4a-46a4-5729-803b-4a8ed45b4b35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f16e8de5-d93f-5c40-b48d-326156982a0f" :answer/id #uuid "f16e8de5-d93f-5c40-b48d-326156982a0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054813 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7712c3e1-7e39-5f21-96a2-73fbade1bb33" "question-adc818d6-3be7-557c-93b2-e7ce26f749ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7712c3e1-7e39-5f21-96a2-73fbade1bb33" :question/id #uuid "7712c3e1-7e39-5f21-96a2-73fbade1bb33" :question/math-academy-id "q-47827" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=-100.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ is constant, its derivative is zero. Therefore, ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6151e229-0e35-564f-8d7f-5b331c2a89a6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6151e229-0e35-564f-8d7f-5b331c2a89a6" :answer-field/id #uuid "6151e229-0e35-564f-8d7f-5b331c2a89a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-fi